			"claims": [
				{
					"id": "correction:15a28e560194b0de108ae4fb20096ea1a92e9dbc1a593d99cc3132592efa3bd1",
					"reason": "For fixed c>0, the supplied proof establishes the genuine operator domain, complete spectrum including 1 and x, and correct sine normalization. Integration by parts gives nonzero k^(-4) leading coefficients for every non-affine named member, with O(k^(-6)) remainders; the spectral series therefore diverges at s=7/2. Independently verified the four-trace determinant 15360. Sobolev approximation followed by its bounded polynomial right inverse yields a D(K_c^2) core; spectral truncation transfers density to 0<=s<7/2. Compatible combinations above the threshold are correctly distinguished from individually admissible members.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6d468ed87a736afdfb81282b1d434d5c0b16a920a59116ca2c4738896d7184f7",
					"reason": "The general scale retains self-adjointness and a strictly positive lower bound. Negative orders are correctly defined by completion, with powers extended as spectral multipliers. In the Krein example, coefficients n^(-1/2) are square-summable with every negative-order spectral weight but not in L2, validating the correction. The bounded/unbounded operator distinction and positive-order isometries are consistent with spectral calculus.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:76ae1aa768a6db16a98db28fb5b738ff2d8556317bb1bd50086601d9ca04b2ed",
					"reason": "The dependency resolves to the supplied current spectral-domain card and fractional proof. The added 0<=s<7/2 statement concerns the fixed Krein sparse family and follows from the separately checked four-trace argument. It introduces no broader hypothesis or conclusion into the abstract self-adjoint scale theorem.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:aa949b7a06836d9ea2713484de2548807e0043e6c6600c5c6c4ce3ced54af7d8",
					"reason": "The criterion explicitly requires membership, an onto isometry, both parity recurrences, pinned low moments, B_j>=0 and A_j-B_j>=4j+c0 for every j>=2. Rewriting the recurrence proves monotonicity and the stated factorial lower bound, including the initial step. Cauchy-Schwarz then eliminates each free moment. The card rejects the invalid A_j-only lower bound and unrestricted high-order extension.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c7080ba7c2ef1b2033b7dcb62e969e37acc23221d74722681cced2d7e1e80794",
					"reason": "The repaired range pointer correctly attributes the additional 3<s<7/2 window to the independent graph-core proof. It does not assert that the moment-jump method works in spaces lacking its test monomials. The endpoint exclusion and exact dependency hashes agree with the checked spectral source.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6bd2127271b8002ba3f637e9fcfa27573d02f993a06ab4405ca1fce982db8440",
					"reason": "Direct moment use is restricted to s=2,3, with test monomials in L2 and the H1 form domain respectively. The displayed coefficients have B>=0 and gap 4m+cm/(m-1)>=4m+c in both parities. Thus the growth argument has the required hypotheses. Formal differential expressions, algebraic inverses and genuine operator powers remain separated, and unrestricted integer-order propagation is withdrawn.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:d5c986e8260e6d53b4e310fb6eff66de8692cdc2079abf36784819368f6ae527",
					"reason": "The current card accurately imports the full nonnegative window through the checked spectral dependency while retaining s=2,3 as the direct scope of its recurrence method. It neither extrapolates H3 density upward nor defines higher-order monomial moments without membership.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:26407866b3eb4034b240ff741a3d270995ad4a1c49b5ebbeb70a2bf89c85151a",
					"reason": "The abstract criteria require all polynomials to belong to, and be dense in, the ambient Hilbert space. Both parity branches and low-moment conditions are retained. The diagonal threshold beta=3/2 follows from the series with terms comparable to m^(2-2beta), including divergence at equality. The card correctly refuses to apply these hypotheses indiscriminately to Krein power domains and limits historical high-order computations to formal evidence.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:22f146c8cda5ae02aad6c635fc0226ec7b8e14c846f6ef9be736be149d692380",
					"reason": "The fractional extension uses the independently checked graph core, without assuming all monomials belong to the target domain. The projection qualification is correct: polynomial density alone does not imply sparse-family density, and adding x^2,x^3 supplies the missing algebraic directions. Finite moment injectivity is appropriately restricted to the finite-dimensional tail obstruction rather than an infinite-dimensional V.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:dfe69aac1cc39c7aba7abc9859d24499f6a52e756a4ad0ec32d81a0dfdaea3e7",
					"reason": "The boundary condition now uses first derivatives and agrees with the supplied operator definitions. The card distinguishes the H1 orthogonal Krein-Sobolev system from the nonorthogonal sparse family and preserves the inherited H2/H3 completeness scope. Its inverse warning is substantiated by the supplied x^2 example: the algebraic inverse violates the boundary condition, whereas the genuine inverse includes a hyperbolic correction. The withdrawn all-order polynomial interpretation is not reinstated.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:8a7029b0cb118701bbba702e962f82d2cb96cce31de7ef87f95ccab72b400bb2",
					"reason": "The Gram identity gives Q_n=(P_n-P_(n-2))/sqrt(2(2n-1)). The ordinary H1 limits are correctly P2/sqrt(6), P3/sqrt(10), and Q_n for fixed n>=4; only their quotient classes have the unified limit [Q_n]. The positive parity recurrence bounds the remainder by O_n(a_n), not O(1), and yields the stated fixed-index asymptotics. Finite polynomial expansions justify the H1 convergence without a uniform-in-n assertion.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4642df3b2057e258d4056d26a993ce0165e3576b022d0af60deec33e7ab4c6f3",
					"reason": "The new window is explicitly assigned to the original sparse family, preserving its distinction from the Krein-Sobolev orthogonal polynomials. Every non-affine named member is excluded at and above 7/2, while finite combinations may cancel boundary residuals. The fixed-c fractional result is not conflated with the separate fixed-index c-to-zero quotient limit.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c704f0b5443243081c96a35469d3649aadace73278c4f2427ecbd550bb77cbf9",
					"reason": "The general recurrence now supplies only a product lower bound; exact diagonal completeness uses both actual recurrence solutions. Product classifications are restricted to B=B'=0, with the correct normalization and critical endpoints. Both perturbed coefficients are included. The all-index bound |delta_m|<=1/(8m) implies the claimed positive gap, whereas the explicit P2 annihilator demonstrates failure for merely bounded or eventually small perturbations. Formal images are correctly separated from operator-domain claims.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:458a02186e9a8e23d76fc42be0faa4d9943d5e073d578c5c72a31781c20a6d4c",
					"reason": "The stability proof binding matches the supplied unchanged source. Its recurrence, diagonal-series and perturbation arguments do not depend on the quotient representative-limit assertion repaired in the other document. Checking these arguments establishes the requested renewal without treating the quotient correction or a previous approval as evidence of stability validity.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:ff0ab3ad28d7a31f6dded0143b838518577b9efa30c664c2882acdf985e88ac7",
					"reason": "The card imports 0<=s<7/2 through the separate fractional proof and keeps the abstract stability hypotheses unchanged. It does not identify coefficient-diagonal spaces with Krein power domains or infer admissibility of perturbed polynomials from formal differentiation. No stronger basis or unconditional perturbation conclusion is introduced.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4660445eefe6a76a2b70658964d090a0e893c9026ec4f396c040753b038c9124",
					"reason": "The structural result is explicitly confined to fixed c>0 and H_c^2=D(K_c), with norm ||K_cf||_2. The supplied proof establishes positivity, surjectivity, Sobolev norm equivalence and continuity of both central traces. It retains the low-moment conditions required for zero-solution rigidity and makes no unsupported higher-order or arbitrary-subfamily density inference.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:cee93c289836f3d9d4fb197a917cfe93c205619d43e7a2b9d1a5d7bdb500126b",
					"reason": "The Green kernels satisfy the half-interval equations, endpoint conditions and interface jumps giving f(0) and f'(0), including correct complex conjugation conventions. The tail closure follows from local zero-trace cutoff estimates, Sobolev polynomial approximation and the invertible endpoint correction matrix of determinant 2L^2. This proves the cofinite classification and refutes the old unconditional claims. The multiplication-by-x^M argument correctly repairs finite monomial deletion, and the odd substitution factor is 1.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:e99563a533bc6c760da7a90f9327742d52c8000206f0f963fb98d1fa5be54e44",
					"reason": "The updated scale dependency matches the supplied current version. The cofinite theorem remains an s=2 result with the same two trace obstructions. Completeness of the full family throughout 0<=s<7/2 is not used to extend deletion classifications, tail realizability or constrained-subspace density to other orders.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "R8-unchanged-card-renewal",
					"reason": "All 85 snapshot hashes match. All 77 inputs of the supplied previous packet are present; 76 retain identical hashes, and only the summary differs. The supplied before-summary bytes match its previous hash, and an independently computed diff confirms the single INF paragraph replacement. The 18 correction claims and their eight target versions match the renewal mappings. Inspection of the mathematical arguments and dependencies finds no changed INF premise in the retained fractional, trace, projection, moment, stability or quotient results. Their restrictions remain intact, and the historical all-order orthogonal-systems interpretation remains withdrawn.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				}
